-- What the vending machines opened in playfield 1186 were selling,
-- read out of the ShopUpdates the live server sent.
--
-- A machine is placed by the playfield file, not by this. What is here is
-- its stock: a vendortemplate row for the machine, and the
-- shopinventorytemplates rows it names.
--
-- The hash is the item template the machine is built from, so it belongs
-- to the machine rather than to this playfield, and every playfield that
-- stands the same machine is stocked by the same rows. The column that
-- holds it was four characters wide, which is not enough for that, so it
-- is widened here too.

ALTER TABLE vendortemplate MODIFY `Hash` varchar(32) NOT NULL;
ALTER TABLE vendortemplate MODIFY `ShopInvHash` varchar(32) NOT NULL;


-- These 62 machines are stood 159 times, across 10 playfields:
--   playfield 500      6 of these machines   Parnassos
--   playfield 655     16 of these machines   Andromeda
--   playfield 1186    62 of these machines   Neutral Supermarket Basic
--   playfield 1187    62 of these machines   Neutral Supermarket Advanced
--   playfield 2060     1 of these machines   neut_basic_weapon _shop
--   playfield 2064     3 of these machines   neut_basic_implants_shop
--   playfield 2070     1 of these machines   neut_advanced_weapons_shop
--   playfield 2073     3 of these machines   neut_advanced_implants_shop
--   playfield 2096     3 of these machines   4holes Fashion
--   playfield 6553     2 of these machines   Arete Landing

-- A vendors row is believed before the machine's own stock is. These stand on
-- a machine this recording measured and were written by hand rather than read
-- off the wire, so they go. A row keyed on a playfield and a statel - the shape
-- this tool writes - came from a recording too, and is left alone.
